      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "BLACK ZOUS (3) gets the nod off the strongest current form: he won a BM76 at this track by just over four lengths two starts back, beating LIMITED RISK, then held third behind Golden Tunes last week despite being slow to begin. His two wins and five placings from seven at this track and distance put him on top. BAHAMA BAY (1) has not been close at his past two, including fourth to Golden Tunes last start, but his 1200m record is deep and Stan Tsaikos has won two from three on him, so he is the main place or winning danger if he sharpens up. TELLEZ (6) is harder to dismiss after winning a BM64 by just over five lengths as a well-supported favourite, though Open grade is a firmer test than that small-field success. BOY BIG (4) ran second at big odds last week and has extensive track-and-trip form; his task is to prove that it was not simply a spike after a heavy defeat the run prior.",
